    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469">

                <pb facs="0853" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg791"/>

                <head>No. 464.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reed to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-06-11"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 11, 1878</date>.
                        (Received July 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: One of the results of the pacification of
                    the Island of Cuba has been the termination, by royal decree, of the sentence of
                    suspension imposed on certain Spanish journals and the withdrawal of all
                    accusations pending’ before the tribunals established under the royal decree of
                    31st December, 1875.</p>
                <p>The royal decree first above mentioned, a copy and translation of which I beg to
                    inclose, appeared in the Gaceta de Madrid of this morning.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DWIGHT T. REED.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d469-a1.xml" xpointer="d469-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
